/target
/regtest-harness/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig

# Local runtime data / wallets (never commit secrets). /data-btc* covers the datadirs the
# Bitcoin dev-stack samples (deploy/zecd.btc-testnet*.toml) document, which sit in the repo
# root because zecd runs on the host there - the entries below catch a datadir's contents but
# not its `.lock`, so without this the directory itself shows up untracked.
/data
/data-btc*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
keys.toml
*.cookie
.cookie
identity.txt
zecd.toml
# Compose sources stack credentials from a .env, so an operator following the instructions
# creates a credential-bearing file. Unanchored (no leading slash), so it matches at EVERY
# level, not just deploy/: compose reads the .env in its *project* directory, which is the
# directory of the first -f file (deploy/ for `-f deploy/docker-compose...`) but the working
# directory when invoked from there, so both locations are live and a rule naming only one
# leaves the other tracked. Ignored in the tracked .gitignore (not just a local
# .git/info/exclude) so it holds in every clone, not only the one it was written in.
.env
.env.*
# ...but the .example templates are intentional (checked-in examples, no real secrets).
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
!/deploy/zecd.toml
__pycache__/
